+//! Goal waiting-guidance agreement between the developer fragment and request tools.
+//!
+//! Every test drives real `/responses` requests through `test_codex` with the
+//! goal extension installed and asserts the exact request count. The fragment
+//! rendered from each sampling step's `WaitingCapabilities` must match what
+//! the same request advertises: the sleep/stdin sentences iff those tools are
+//! present, the native wait sentence with the actual dotted tool name, and the
+//! negative exec sentence whenever no completion wake can be promised.
+//!
+//! Two architectural facts shape the expectations. Turn-context contributions
+//! are recorded once per turn, before the first sampling request, while the
+//! tool router is rebuilt for every sampling request: a goal created by a
+//! tool mid-turn is therefore visible in the follow-up request's tools one
+//! request before the fragment arrives with the next turn's contribution
+//! (pinned as a known bound in
+//! `waiting_guidance_tool_created_goal_reacts_at_next_turn`). And the V1
+//! native wait tool is deferred behind tool search by default, so fixtures
+//! without a discovery step agree on its absence; only the discovery test
+//! carries the native sentence.
+//!
+//! Request counts stay exact because no automatic goal continuation can fire
+//! after the final turn: tool-driven tests end with the goal completed, while
+//! the service-set tests skip the live-manager rebind, so continuation is
+//! structurally impossible there and the production turn-start reconcile
+//! still publishes the goal marker for the first request.
+#![allow(clippy::unwrap_used)]
+
